  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The full test suite passes: 1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/core.py`, a subcommand's context now takes only its own entry from the parent's map (`parent.default_map.get(info_name)`) instead of the whole map. So `default_map={\"sub\": {\"name\": \"x\"}}` now reaches `sub`'s `--name` option.\n- **Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` to `tests/test_defaults.py`. It covers a plain subcommand and a subcommand inside a nested group.\n\nI only ran the full suite after the change, so I haven't seen the new test fail without the fix.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
